# Web Push (VAPID) — public key only.
#
# Next.js only exposes variables prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ to the browser, and inlines
# them into the JavaScript bundle at build time. This must be the URL-safe base64
# PUBLIC key of the VAPID pair (an ~87-character string that starts with "B").
#
# The PRIVATE half is a secret: it belongs ONLY in the Supabase Edge Function
# secret VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY read by `send-push`. Never add it here or to any
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable — those end up in every visitor's browser.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and paste your public key after the "=". Set the
# same variable in your hosting provider's environment settings for production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=

# Supabase service-role key — SERVER ONLY.
#
# The organisation IP allowlist is evaluated by public.ip_guard, which is granted
# to `service_role` only. Middleware and the sign-in handler call it through a
# service-role client, so this key must be present in the server environment.
#
# It bypasses row-level security and must NEVER be prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ or
# otherwise exposed to the browser. Next.js only inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables
# into the client bundle; this one stays on the server.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
